Package: dvbtx
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: BILLY Rémi <byhoster.association@gmail.com>
Section: video
Priority: optional
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), ffmpeg, tzdata, @DEPENDS@
Recommends: @RECOMMENDS@
Suggests: tsduck, hackrf, uhd-host, streamlink, yt-dlp, dvb-tools, avahi-utils
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/TrusterBSW/DVB-Tx
Description: DVB head-end on software radios (HackRF, USRP, SoapySDR), closed coax
 dvbtx builds complete DVB multiplexes from live streams (HLS, RTMP, SRT,
 YouTube, Twitch, M3U, tvheadend), capture devices (webcam, HDMI capture,
 screen), files and pipes, and modulates them on software radios: DVB-T,
 DVB-T2, DVB-C, DVB-S and DVB-S2/S2X, mixed on one radio, any number of
 multiplexes per radio and of radios, each bound to its device by serial
 number, configured in one TOML file, on the command line or on a web page.
 .
 The C engine multiplexes on the modulator clock (exact rate, PCR restamped,
 automatic switch to a backup clip), builds PSI/SI (NIT with logical channel
 numbers, SDT, EIT from XMLTV, TOT) and synthesises all the carriers of a
 radio together. A web page shows the bit rates, the decoding margin of every
 service and the alerts; the TSDuck analysis can be exported as JSON.
 .
 Radiating on broadcast frequencies is forbidden: closed coax only.
